{"title":"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(coordbash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (coordbash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5(Analytical_geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5(Analytical geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Fast_+_Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Fast + Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three unit squares and two line segments connecting two pairs of vertices are shown. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344ad68ce1c966777c56c860c4fc9b0da8bb06cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(1,0); pair C=(0.8,-0.4); draw(A--(2,0)); draw((0,-1)--(2,-1)); draw((0,-2)--(1,-2)); draw(A--(0,-2)); draw(B--(1,-2)); draw((2,0)--(2,-1)); draw(A--(2,-1)); draw(B--(0,-2));  pair[] ps={A,B,C}; dot(ps);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); [/asy]\" width=\"198\" height=\"208\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749b5e02653b37be898f1bea53180cd04c8a6eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac15 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac29 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac13 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"382\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2962535eca035d3778df987a78828ddda1ef94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(1,0); pair C=(0.8,-0.4); pair D=(1,-2), E=(0,-2); draw(A--(2,0)); draw((0,-1)--(2,-1)); draw(E--D); draw(A--E); draw(B--D); draw((2,0)--(2,-1)); draw(A--(2,-1)); draw(B--E);  pair[] ps={A,B,C,D,E}; dot(ps); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(D--E),S); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(A--B),N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(A--E),W); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{5}$&quot;,(B--E),NW); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"228\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at a right angle, (this can be proved by noticing that the slopes of the two lines are negative reciprocals of each other) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e511a9c9ae68ff2929b87efa8323f24033e15a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle BED$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />. The hypotenuse of right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c0afb40c0a08457a36ebab89b23c17b40b9eff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/c/d7c102e6d465673a7871e64ea35e2c43eeabc419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/0150847710c03762e544bcc9613888d3bb87c8ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AC}{BC}=\\frac{BD}{ED} \\Rightarrow \\frac{AC}{BC} = \\frac21 \\Rightarrow AC=2BC\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cbb6282231d3ac6d83e3d38ecb4d13e4a76955b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AC}{AB}=\\frac{BD}{BE} \\Rightarrow \\frac{AC}{1}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\Rightarrow AC=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297ae6ae813c551d1393d02eab6c61224c33b9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=2BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd37f9eb7cdd5eafd97400a161d7d5d535789e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"80\" height=\"41\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle so the area is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/3637a1c6dcce1975d4ea8e49b501b3389de09541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12 \\cdot AC \\cdot BC = \\frac12 \\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"299\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28coordbash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(coordbash)\">Solution 2 (coordbash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (coordbash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39df2e0f6418671630036f076cb8d2c2353be73f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(1,0); pair C=(0.8,-0.4); pair D=(1,-2), E=(0,-2); pair F=(2,-1); pair G=(0.8,0); draw(A--(2,0)); draw((0,-1)--F); draw(E--D); draw(A--E); draw(B--D); draw((2,0)--F); draw(A--F); draw(B--E); draw(C--G);  pair[] ps={A,B,C,D,E,F,G}; dot(ps);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,E); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,N); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"228\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5bb2aa78132b4b716cfde4a9136c884d94c753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{E}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> be the origin. Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/675f328c54ec0f5717f06ed2c59eaa73ebfe5d64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}=(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/176c18deba24cc458583eff8c7c07888b0b5f225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}=(0, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/935bd30c8f66d884e6384b74e2f2274f355e2ff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}=(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3da76346d81b9959d5e5ba52a4cfe36a84f084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{F}=(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117d4d0095663b58e00a82f9a89cedc6db1ac00f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${EB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> can be represented by the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c311147b479df529d837e7da1ff0428df1f75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />\nAlso, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c4227cb24a0b9437e1712c84868a216d1470cfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${AF}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> can be represented by the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50dca1a70ec85484063dd28a476c5838124b86a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the second equation from the first gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebbaeb87e5728806c15e3f21bcf59f8b79669c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}x-2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />. \nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dc21b2e5ed3b50a84a2630b387daabf2f9f958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />.\nPlugging this into the first equation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/84828310e7a4c598c5cf60977078ae5e2b1521db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/2344c11792dfb801dae4fac625f17e9652085b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{C} (0.8, 1.6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/391e7d39dd970d63d1ec1854c1c5a97ad7050883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0.8, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fce52291eb23844454c6e5d33d1bfd2157c31625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${AB}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524130326fdf82a03c479e485f196159e29abc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${CG}=0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b0a794ca64c1958b51615daee0e4acd6840376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot {AB} \\cdot {CG}=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 0.4=0.2=\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"352\" height=\"37\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80750f389b1273d2ea4df0d66fbdd7fce777f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>Note: Once you have determined that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/2344c11792dfb801dae4fac625f17e9652085b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{C} (0.8, 1.6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, you can use Shoelace Theorem to determine the area of triangle ABC.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/e/9de7e0273e04ad8bd29e5a7990f53d6bafc21be6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(1,0); pair C=(0.8,-0.4); pair D=(1,-2), E=(0,-2); pair F=(2,-1); pair G=(0.8,0); pair H=(0,-1), I=(0.5,-1);  draw(A--(2,0)); draw((0,-1)--F); draw(E--D); draw(A--E); draw(B--D); draw((2,0)--F); draw(A--F); draw(B--E); draw(C--G); draw(H--I);  pair[] ps={A,B,C,D,E,F,G, H, I}; dot(ps);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,E); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,N); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,W); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,E); [/asy]\" width=\"222\" height=\"228\" /></center>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e30e7dec97a3f5e84e0de8a12e3056c6c9a77fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EAB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4fa9bc2747b36eaeb99bf3bbcb87d9852800271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EHI$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />; line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99af1405ade3d02aee1931a255c7769587072f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HI = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21361fc8f29984fa3e95bfc0e578efdbce08c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3ece5b999db15471c68e0626a16947db526d50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> and the ratio of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe087e026658a3a6d554b9de55d1d34bb0cc475e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF = 1 : \\frac{3}{2} = 2: 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Based on similarity the length of the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68ebf9f9ddef66e02f09fcf82b59f6c54ec2bb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/12086d9367148066ba80a51a78734754b677760b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot1 = \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5278a1fb6b0e30093e722749c855c2b6bace0a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot {AB} \\cdot {CG}=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"294\" height=\"37\" />. \nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80750f389b1273d2ea4df0d66fbdd7fce777f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the diagonal and the end of the unit square meet, on the right side of the diagram. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the top right corner of the top right unit square, where segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/25697024d81a441f727e279d2216eeb169abced9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABL$\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> is 2 units in length.\n</p><p>Because of the Pythagorean Theorem, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286e989082359d570543d0269004ce484008ce68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7097b70b28f5c53561a0e5a72a06d96bfeb90bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LK$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> = 1, the diagonal of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c1d0f56288cc1df7d344f97265647c91ee4825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ALK$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nTriangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c1d0f56288cc1df7d344f97265647c91ee4825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ALK$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is clearly a similar triangle to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the hypotenuse of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. So, we can write down:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/8088e9c9db130f3d12b9dec7f02ec50c37f78530.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AK/AB = LK/BC\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, which is equal to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19dbf7d361a8bb1d07b5886872fc142cee9245ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{1} = \\frac{1}{BC}\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"41\" /> Solving this equation yields:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f2e87f2c99bd6a6ba3bfe6c821032e5248bc61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>By Pythagorean theorem, we can now find segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/8282f9b811cf4f5094628e40b98776713911d82b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})^2 + AC^2 = 1\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" /> Solving this yields:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006b18f5ffa53bbf7b3dc4ceb7ccba857ee55f6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = \\frac{4}{5}\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c7dc8464b72f93e08e0674b645f5d48ccc0336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>So then we can use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75e777bb82b58500cede2c9fac65d894813155c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\frac{1}{2} * b * a.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"37\" />\nSo  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e7210128280821fa969fd11da63a37aa38e6fa53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\frac{1}{2} * \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} *  \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/2/662f76a72f9614a5c67129e440669bffa3e96631.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac15}\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5.28Analytical_geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5(Analytical_geometry)\">Solution 5(Analytical geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5(Analytical geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line segment ending at B can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c311147b479df529d837e7da1ff0428df1f75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, where the bottom left corner of the bottom square is the origin. The line segment ending at A can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cbb49f9027843662f3d3d8541b3fcadf52ba351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-1/2 x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. Solving for x and y, we get the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bace3d430532625952bb07b658b9306aa1d0c364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4/5, 8/5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> for the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. In this system, line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has a height of 2. Therefore, the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e767d082e87040b6c72f30717c140928d8e1a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2- 8/5=2/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />. Finding the area of the triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c5ad2672600f755efc51e9f41508b97cbac7535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2*1*2/5=\\boxed{1/5=B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"202\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Fast_.2B_Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Fast_+_Intuitive)\">Solution 6 (Fast + Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Fast + Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the figure in Solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791e46e2e6340c71cdfe421007efddf790f14cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBD \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. Using the pythagorean theorem, we find that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c4e1c8ebc027d8a09149acca4fbbc994bcca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB = \\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" /> .\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a649aee592a9c37d2f9b5d5239f5e06e533130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> ,\nthe ratio of the triangles' sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae26d1d19e9371dd57975f8cc1eb7c580626ad25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" />.\nThis means that the ratio of their areas are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b76f8e29524b1dcf49fa8069ba5b2e722c5eb12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{1/5=B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"165\" height=\"48\" /> \n~UsernamePasswordPassword\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HVesU8cTjRU\">https://youtu.be/HVesU8cTjRU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=1717\">https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=1717</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A\">2012 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\